Subject: [PATCH] routing: an account removed from its provider leaves the
 Accounts and keys fold (#5895)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The fold on the Routing page built its list from two places that keep
what a provider served: the day's tallies (#3351), and the orders of the
requests the gateway still keeps. An account removed from its provider
(WorkBuddy's third, its five failed tries on the day) stayed listed with
"what's left not known yet", and the fold heading counted it in "{n}
accounts" and "{n} available" for the rest of the day.

The history read the live page already polls now carries what each
provider serves now (`serves`), named the way the tallies and the fold
name them: an account by its provider and its user in lower case, a key
or the provider by its own id — a key's alone when it is the only one,
with its own when there are more (provider.AccountIDs, so a plugin's
accounts are all there). The fold keeps its entries to those, live; a
day looked at keeps who it had.

Tests: routing-acts-removed (chromium + webkit) — a provider routed over
three accounts, its third removed: gone from the list, the fold row
counting three gone with it, the others' counts still the day's. Ablated
twice: the fold's keep-to-served filter taken out, the removed account
back on the page; the `serves` line taken out of the read,
TestLiveHistoryServesWhatTheProvidersServeNow red. That test locks the
key forms and a key's removal on the Go side, and a day asked by name
carrying no such list.

Fixes #5895

